  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0007_9ada87a4db95.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 119px;\" /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0007_4ba8391a3a75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 449px; height: 177px;\" /><br /><br /><br />There are four different (A, B, C and D) monochloro products.<br />&nbsp;<table align=\"center\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\t<thead>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">&nbsp;</th>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">&nbsp;</th>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">&nbsp;</th>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">Relative amount</th>\t\t</tr>\t</thead>\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(A)</td>\t\t\t<td><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0007_4fa25fc94085.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 143px; height: 96px;\" /></strong></u></td>\t\t\t<td>(A) is obtained from the reaction of three equivalent <math> <mrow> <msup> <mn>1</mn> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> H atoms.</td>\t\t\t<td>3 x 1 = 3.0</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(B)</td>\t\t\t<td><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0007_7210e213d8f9.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 113px; height: 111px;\" /></strong></u></td>\t\t\t<td>(B) is obtained from the reaction of two equivalent <math> <mrow> <msup> <mn>2</mn> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> H atoms.</td>\t\t\t<td>2 x 3.8 = 7.6</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(C)</td>\t\t\t<td><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0007_26e307271639.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 137px; height: 97px;\" /></strong></u></td>\t\t\t<td>(C) is obtained from the reaction of one equivalent <math> <mrow> <msup> <mn>3</mn> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> H atoms.</td>\t\t\t<td>1 x 5 = 5.0</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(D)</td>\t\t\t<td><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0007_28113d3c0406.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 132px; height: 128px;\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0007_14de0c5c3084.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 98px; height: 101px;\" /></td>\t\t\t<td>(D) is obtained from the reaction of six equivalent <math> <mrow> <msup> <mn>1</mn> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> H atoms.</td>\t\t\t<td><br />\t\t\t6 x 1 = 6.0<br />\t\t\t<br />\t\t\t<br />\t\t\tTotal = 21.6</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><br /><br />Therefore, percentages of the A, B, C and D monochloro products are as follows :<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>A</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>1</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>3</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>9</mn> <mo>&asymp;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>%</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>B</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>1</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mn>5</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>1</mn> <mn>8</mn> <mo>&asymp;</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mn>5</mn> <mtext>%</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>C</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>5</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>1</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mn>3</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>1</mn> <mn>5</mn> <mo>&asymp;</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mn>3</mn> <mtext>%</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>D</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>6</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>1</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mn>7</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>8</mn> <mo>&asymp;</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mn>8</mn> <mtext>%</mtext> </mrow> </math>"
  }
